<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Andahuaylas</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Andahuaylas is a town in the Apurímac region of the southern Peruvian Andes, west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cusco">Cusco</a> on the old route to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayacucho">Ayacucho</a>. Before the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inca-empire">Incas</a> it was the heart of the Chanka confederation, whose attack on Cusco around 1438, by Inca tradition, prompted the rise of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pachacuti">Pachacuti</a>. Under Spanish rule it was an important colonial town of the southern highlands.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/andahuaylas.jpg" alt="Andahuaylas" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nino sanchez carojo · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Andahuaylas_-2025.35.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
